---

The calls — cURL reference

Once pasted, this is exactly what the client hits:

List supported platforms (public, no auth):

```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/api/social/platforms
```

Connect Instagram to store #1:

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/stores/1/social \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -b cookies.txt \
  -d '{"platform":"instagram","handle":"tedcoffee"}'
```

List connected accounts:

```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/api/stores/1/social -b cookies.txt
```

Request verification code:

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/stores/1/social/1/verify/request -b cookies.txt
# → { "code": "TED-A1B2C3", "instructions": "Post this code publicly on your Instagram profile..." }
```

Confirm verification (after posting the code):

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/stores/
curl http://localhost:3000/api/social/platforms
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/stores/1/social \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -b cookies.txt \
  -d '{"platform":"instagram","handle":"tedcoffee"}'
curl http://localhost:3000/api/stores/1/social -b cookies.txt
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/stores/1/social/1/verify/request -b cookies.txt
# → { "code": "TED-A1B2C3", "instructions": "Post this code publicly on your Instagram profile..." }
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/stores/1/social/1/verify/confirm -b cookies.txt
curl -X PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/stores/1/social/1 \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" -b cookies.txt \
  -d '{"handle":"ted_coffee_lab"}'
curl -X DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/stores/1/social/1 -b cookies.txt
curl http://localhost:3000/api/stores/ted-coffee/social

